  "limitations": "This does not complete MR-10 or the 17-package goal. Native S3 seed selection/install, full native joined-node restart/crash qualification and the remaining recovery fault matrix are still open. Trusted physical endpoints are preconfigured; this is explicit learner admission, without automatic placement, promotion or repair. The stable joined-state drill reopens the real engine and ImageApplier; it does not claim a complete public Node restart/replacement controller. The internal protocol identity cellar-raft-ltx-1/members-1/seeds-1 refuses earlier checksum-valid namespace roots; format markers remain 1, with no compatibility reader or migration. Use a fresh experimental namespace/prefix and local state. Object storage is in-memory. Current Node coverage is the affected Raft lifecycle case; earlier 304-case/88-Node evidence remains a separate historical source qualification. Seven ignored child entry points run through owning parents and are excluded. No physical S3, power loss, zones, production performance/capacity, larger-scale tiers, federation or complete release qualification is claimed. Existing vendored warnings remain visible.",
